> In this model, coastal damages include the loss of land and immobile capital to permanent inundation; the costs of retreat (relocating people and movable assets, demolishing buildings, and associated intangible relocation losses); the costs of protection (building and maintaining levees and the land they occupy); and the loss of wetlands due to sea-level rise or protection structures. It also includes expected annual damages from extreme sea level events, both to capital (via depth–damage relationships) and to human life (valued using a value-of-statistical-life approach).
